---
description: Next.js 16 App Router conventions
globs: apps/web/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Rendering
- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only for: state, effects, event handlers, browser-only libs (charts, d3, portals).
- Pass serializable data into client children.

# Routing
- Use route groups `(app)` / `(marketing)` for layout separation (already present).
- Route handlers (`app/api/**/route.ts`) should stay thin and avoid business logic.

# Components
- Prefer simple functional components.
- Prefer `@astraq/ui` primitives and semantic theme tokens over one-off styling.
- Keep reusable styles and component logic easy to find and maintain.
- Keep local UI state local.

# Charts
- Prefer chart choices that fit financial data well and stay performant with larger series.
- Distinguish clearly between historical and predicted data.
- Handle resizing and rerendering carefully; chart interactions should stay smooth.

# Caching
- Do not disable caching globally; opt-out per request with `cache: 'no-store'` when data is user-specific.

# Do not
- Do not import server-only code (`env.ts`, SDK server bindings) from a `"use client"` file.
- Do not call `cookies()`/`headers()` outside Server Components or route handlers.
